{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 (rebar-debug) — ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED (runtime-proven, offline + live).\n\n## Mechanism (single root cause)\nThe DC rich-text failures are a SYMPTOM of a `sync --only`-generic apply-dispatch drop — NOT a codec/differ/overlay defect. Under the PRIMARY route `sync --only=<local_id>,<key>` (Mode.LIVE, route=\"sync\", selection_ids set), an outbound scalar UPDATE on a BOUND issue is planned as `scope_deferred` and never written; the legacy route `--mode live --filter-local-ids` writes it correctly.\n\nChain:\n- run_differs builds the outbound update and appends the typed Mutation with `target = om.jira_key` (the Jira KEY) — run_differs.py:582-599.\n- run_differs.py:293-302 calls `ticket_planner.plan_pass(selection={\"kind\": selection_kind, \"ids\": sorted(selection_ids)})` — the ids are the SELECTED LOCAL IDS only.\n- `ticket_planner._scope_excluded(target, selection)` (ticket_planner.py:95) does `target not in ids` for kind=\"only\". For an update, target is the JIRA KEY but ids are LOCAL IDS, so the in-scope bound-issue update is classified out-of-scope → `_classify_early` returns `PlanDisposition.defer / scope_deferred` (ticket_planner.py:124).\n- `batch_dispatch.reroute_migrated_plans` counts the deferred plan as migrated, EXCLUDES its real mutation dict from the legacy `_apply_batch` loop, and hands it to `coordinate_and_fuse`, whose coordinator SKIPS any non-`mutate` plan without calling execute. Net: the write is dropped (deferred_count=1); handle_update / update_issue / Issue.update never fire.\n\nThe legacy `--filter-local-ids` route works because it scopes via `_build_filter_target_set` (reconcile_helpers.py), which expands to LOCAL IDS ∪ their BOUND JIRA KEYS, so `_mutation_matches_filter` matches jira-key-targeted updates. The primary route's planner scope check never got that expansion. Because the description write never lands, remote stays None and every subsequent pass re-derives description!=wire and re-emits — the perpetual re-push (symptom 2) and empty render (symptom 1) both follow from the dropped write.\n\n## Proof (discriminating, runtime)\n- Live in-CI agentic probe (run 33129851229) instrumented in-subprocess: under `sync --only`, breadcrumb `RECON: outbound_update changed=[description]` fires but handle_update / _IssuesMixin.update_issue / _update_one_scalar_update / Issue.update NEVER fire (ev-0033/0036/0037/0038/0048), remote stays None (ev-0049); the same value via Mode.LIVE `--filter-local-ids` applies (\"OK: applied 1 of 1\", ev-0041/0042) and the next `sync --only` pass then reports outbound_differ total=0 (ev-0043/0044). Summary drops the same way (ev-0039/0040), proving it is not rich-text-specific.\n- Offline deterministic reproduction (fake transport, this worktree): Route A `selection_kind=\"only\", route=\"sync\"` → update_issue NOT fired; Route B `filter_local_ids` → `update_issue(DIG-1) fields=['description']` fired. Trace shows the plan disposition is `defer` (A) vs `mutate` (B); the mutation is identical after run_differs on both routes.\n\n## Attribution\n`--class=regression`, `--caused-by=67d4-ecba-cf95-4353` (commit d49466b5 \"Wire live coordinator+fuse non-create reroute\", 2026-08-25). The defective scope check (`_scope_excluded` comparing a jira-key target against a local-id selection) was authored shadow-only in 85f8-de1a-e425-4584 (commit 6bcf548d, plan-lifecycle planner) where it only fed a parity comparison and dropped nothing. It became a live WRITE DROP when 67d4 made the coordinator+fuse reroute the authoritative dispatch path for non-create mutations without ensuring in-scope bound-issue updates classify as `mutate`. Before 67d4, `sync --only` applied updates via the legacy `_apply_batch` loop; 67d4 is the change a reviewer could have caught the drop in. Divergence from a whole-file blame majority noted: the fix lands in run_differs/ticket_planner, but the regression is attributed to the reroute cutover that activated the latent scope-check defect.\n\n## Fix (Phase 2)\nExpand the selection ids handed to the planner to LOCAL IDS ∪ their BOUND JIRA KEYS (parity with the legacy `_build_filter_target_set`), so a bound-issue update (target=jira_key) is recognized in-scope and planned `mutate`. RED oracle: a scoped `sync --only` pass with a bound-issue scalar drift must dispatch the write (currently RED for `--only`, GREEN for `--filter-local-ids`)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787880001546188001,"uuid":"4d50cf0a-1371-4f49-bc6b-df80ebb93844"}